    <h1>About</h1>
    <p class="lede">Associate Professor of Design at the University of Palermo. Researcher, designer
       and social entrepreneur.</p>
  </header>

  <section aria-labelledby="bio">
    <h2 id="bio">Biography</h2>
    <figure class="portrait">
      <picture>
        <source srcset="/assets/img/portrait.avif" type="image/avif">
        <img src="/assets/img/portrait.webp" width="640" height="640" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
             alt="Salvatore Di Dio, smiling, in a dark jacket and white shirt against a light grey wall.">
      </picture>
      <figcaption>Photo © PUSH, <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/filippimauro/">Mauro Filippi</a></figcaption>
    </figure>
    <p>I was born in Palermo in 1983, and I still live and work here. I'm Caterina's husband and
       Bruna's dad.</p>
    <p>I teach design at the University of Palermo, where I am an Associate Professor. My research
       sits at the intersection of social innovation, environmental sustainability, and new media and
       technologies.
       Underneath it there is one question, easy to ask and hard to answer: why do people who know
       the climate is changing still take the car every morning? I have been designing for that gap
       since 2012.</p>
    <p>It started with <a href="https://www.ponrec.it/open-data/risultati/social-innovation/pon04a3_00451/">trafficO2</a>,
       a game on students' phones that I coordinated with €1.25M from the Italian Ministry of
       Education and Research. After being accelerated by
       <a href="https://archinect.com/news/article/101575299/30-weeks-an-experimental-new-design-school-backed-by-google">30 Weeks</a>,
       the programme of Google and Hyper Island, it grew into MUV2020, a
       <a href="https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/723521">Horizon 2020 project</a> with 14 partners
       in 8 countries that I coordinated, and then
       into <a href="/projects/#muv">MUV</a>, a University of Palermo spin-off that turns sustainable
       mobility into a sport. Played in over 25 cities, it has cut participants' CO<sub>2</sub> by
       33.8% on average, measured with an algorithm certified by RINA to ISO 14064-II.</p>
    <p>I rarely work alone. In 2013, with friends, I founded <a href="/projects/#push">PUSH</a>, a
       non-profit design lab in Palermo, and <a href="/projects/#piranesi">The Piranesi
       Experience</a>, a documentary company whose films have reached Tribeca and Rotterdam. Over
       the years I have learned that a good idea needs three things: a lab to test it, a platform
       to measure it and a story to carry it.</p>
    <p>I have published over 50 scientific contributions and spoken twice at TEDx. I hold a PhD in
       energy and environmental applied physics from the University of Palermo, with a research
       period at MIT in 2012, and I am an Aspen Junior Fellow Alumnus.</p>
  </section>

